indicate the position of the pixel from the end.;
#X text 240 463 @slice FROM TO STEP: Selects all pixels starting from
FROM up to and including TO with the specified STEP. For example \,
if STEP is 3 \, it selects every third pixel in the specified range.;
#X text 240 533 The second type of slices: @lslice. It differs in that
the second parameter represents the LENGTH of the range \, instead
of the last element.;
